<title>INDIA: India NOCIL 96/97 1st half net down.</title>
<headline>India NOCIL 96/97 1st half net down.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	  445.1	 vs    491.1</p>
<p>    Net sales	 6,120.6	 vs  5,961.7</p>
<p>    Shr (in rupees) *   7.26	vs     16.02</p>
<p>    Other income	225.0	 vs    232.3</p>
<p>    Expenditure     5,303.0	 vs  5,015.0</p>
<p>    Interest	    345.9	 vs    292.8</p>
<p>    Depreciation	 81.6	 vs     74.3</p>
<p>    Tax		   170.0	 vs    320.8</p>
<p>Note: Petrochemicals firm National Organic Chemical Industries Ltd (NOCIL), managed by the private Arvind Mafatlal Group, said it approved an interim dividend of 10 percent.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom -91-22-265 9000</p>
